# Vendored skill files are hash-locked against their exact bytes (skills/SKILLS.lock.json, tree_sha256 /
# read_bytes()). Without this file, GitHub-hosted windows-latest runners default to core.autocrlf=true and
# actions/checkout converts every text file to CRLF on checkout, producing different bytes than the LF content
# committed to the repository and failing `maf-harness lint-skills` on that matrix leg every run. Force LF on
# checkout on every platform so the working tree always matches what is hashed.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# cmd.exe needs CRLF (labels/goto break on LF); shell launchers need LF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.command text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
